<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="001" project="spaarke-daily-update-service-r5">
  <metadata>
    <title>OData naming convention doc in docs/standards/ (FR-C9 part 1)</title>
    <phase>0: Quick fixes</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <estimated-hours>1</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>none</dependencies>
    <blocks>002</blocks>
    <tags>docs, standards</tags>
    <rigor-hint>MINIMAL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Documentation task — no code implementation, no tests.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Routine documentation authoring with an explicit convention statement and examples to reproduce; no architectural judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>F</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Create a new standards document at docs/standards/ODATA-NAMING-CONVENTION.md that states the Spaarke OData
    naming convention: binding a lookup via @odata.bind uses the PascalCase attribute SchemaName; filtering or
    selecting a scalar uses the lowercase attribute LogicalName. Include one correct and one incorrect @odata.bind
    example. This is FR-C9 part 1 and unblocks the grep audit in task 002.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer authoring a cross-cutting standards document. Familiar with Dataverse Web API OData
    conventions (LogicalName vs SchemaName) and the existing docs/standards/ style.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A new file docs/standards/ODATA-NAMING-CONVENTION.md exists that states BOTH naming rules (PascalCase SchemaName
    for @odata.bind lookup binding; lowercase LogicalName for filtering/selecting), shows one correct and one
    incorrect @odata.bind example, and is linked from docs/standards/INDEX.md.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      R7 W12 discovered a class of bug where lookups were bound via @odata.bind using the lowercase attribute
      LogicalName (e.g. "sprk_assignedto@odata.bind"), which Dataverse rejects with an OData 400 — the navigation
      property name must be the PascalCase SchemaName ("sprk_AssignedTo"). One instance was fixed in R7
      (useInlineTodoCreate.ts); another remains in EventDetailSidePane (deferred). This doc codifies the convention
      so the pattern is documented once and enforceable, and it is the reference cited by the task-002 grep audit.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>docs/standards/ODATA-NAMING-CONVENTION.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/INDEX.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/CODING-STANDARDS.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">The doc MUST state both rules verbatim in substance: (1) "binding a lookup via @odata.bind -> PascalCase SchemaName"; (2) "filtering or selecting a scalar -> lowercase LogicalName". Do not add rules beyond these two plus the worked examples.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Match the existing docs/standards/ file style (title header, Purpose/Audience header block, markdown tables/code fences) as used by CODING-STANDARDS.md and DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Add exactly one row for the new doc to the docs/standards/INDEX.md "Standards Index" table. Do not restructure INDEX.md otherwise.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">This is a docs-only task. Do NOT modify any source code, deploy scripts, or the EventDetailSidePane files.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-daily-update-service-r5/notes/inbound-from-r7/04-latent-bugs.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-daily-update-service-r5/notes/inbound-from-r7/03-code-review-followups.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/INDEX.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/CODING-STANDARDS.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Standards doc style" location="docs/standards/CODING-STANDARDS.md">
        Header block (Purpose/Audience/Last Reviewed), section headings, fenced code blocks for correct/incorrect examples.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read note 04-latent-bugs.md "Grep audit / Convention documentation" section and note 03 for the source of the convention text and the correct-usage reference sites (SmartTodoWidget.tsx:759, SmartToDo.tsx:680, TodoDetail.tsx:636, useInlineTodoCreate.ts:263).</step>
    <step order="2">Read docs/standards/CODING-STANDARDS.md and DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md to match the header block and section style.</step>
    <step order="3">Write docs/standards/ODATA-NAMING-CONVENTION.md: header block; a "The rule" section stating both rules; a "Where each is used" section (LogicalName in FetchXml / QueryExpression Filter / ColumnSet / $select; SchemaName in @odata.bind navigation-property names and $expand); a "Examples" section with one correct fenced @odata.bind example (PascalCase, e.g. "sprk_AssignedTo@odata.bind") and one incorrect fenced example (lowercase, e.g. "sprk_assignedto@odata.bind") annotated as wrong with the 400-error symptom.</step>
    <step order="4">Add one row to the docs/standards/INDEX.md Standards Index table linking ODATA-NAMING-CONVENTION.md with a one-line description and today's date.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status to completed.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">docs/standards/ODATA-NAMING-CONVENTION.md</output>
    <output type="docs">docs/standards/INDEX.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">docs/standards/ODATA-NAMING-CONVENTION.md exists.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The doc states the @odata.bind -> PascalCase SchemaName rule AND the filter/select -> lowercase LogicalName rule.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The doc contains exactly one correct @odata.bind example (PascalCase SchemaName navigation property) and one incorrect @odata.bind example (lowercase LogicalName) clearly labelled correct vs incorrect.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">docs/standards/INDEX.md contains a link to ODATA-NAMING-CONVENTION.md in its Standards Index table.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No file outside docs/standards/ is modified by this task.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Source convention text is in note 04-latent-bugs.md ("Convention documentation" bullet). The correct SchemaName
    for the recurring example is sprk_AssignedTo. Keep the doc short and focused — two rules plus examples; do not
    expand into a broader Dataverse OData tutorial.
  </notes>

